# BugBug selectors (`data-testid`)

BugBug's preferred locator is a **product-owned test attribute**. Use `data-testid` on every actionable control. Do not rely on copy, CSS classes, Radix/React Aria ids, or DOM position.

Enforced on push: `npm run verify:bugbug-selectors` (`.husky/pre-push`).

## Must have `data-testid`

Buttons, links used as actions, inputs, textareas, checkboxes, switches, radios, selects (`SelectTrigger` / `SelectItem`), dropdown items, dialogs (`DialogContent` + close), collapsible/popover triggers, clickable rows, address-book rows and triggers.

## Naming

`{flow}-{control}` in camelCase after the hyphen, already used in this repo:

```tsx
<Button data-testid="quote-sendButton">…</Button>
<Input data-testid="quoteShipping-zipCode" />
<DialogContent data-testid="addressSelector-dialog" closeTestId="addressSelector-closeButton">
<button type="button" data-testid={`addressSelector-item-${address.id}`}>
<button type="button" data-testid={`shipping-item-${address.id}`} data-country={address.country}>
```

Reuse the same prefix when a form is mounted twice (`quoteShipping-*` vs `quoteBilling-*`, `shipping-*` vs `billing-*`).

## Do not

- Use `data-bugbug-*`, generated ids, or translated text as the primary locator
- Leave clickable `<div>`s — use `<button type="button">` (or a real control) **and** `data-testid`
- Skip a control because Playwright/Jest can find it by role; BugBug still needs the attribute
